  "tagline": {
    "en": "Central, easy, on the BTS. The default for a first visit."
  },
  "about": {
    "en": "Sukhumvit Road runs east from the city centre under the BTS Sukhumvit line, and the sois (side streets) off it hold most of the hotels, condos and restaurants a first visitor ends up in. Nana (BTS E3) is the busiest and loudest part, Asok (E4, with the MRT interchange) is the crossroads, and Phrom Phong (E5) is the calm, upscale end with the big malls and Benjasiri Park. Stay here if you want a hotel on the train line, food at every price, and no need to plan transport."
  },
